inute build step. To meet 30: build each architecture on its own native runner.\"\n  workflow \".github/workflows/coverage.yml\"\n    over-limit-job coverage-build\n      timeout-minutes 40\n      reason \"One instrumented build of every test target, measured 20.5 minutes at most (median 18.1); its 1500s budget needs the 40-minute cap under the 70% share rule (issue #1081). To meet 30: build the unit, integration and source harnesses in parallel jobs.\"\n  workflow \".github/workflows/dependencies-latest.yml\"\n    over-limit-job update\n      timeout-minutes 90\n      reason \"Weekly schedule and dispatch only: updates every dependency, then builds and tests the whole crate in one job.\"\n  workflow \".github/workflows/desktop-release.yml\"\n    over-limit-job build\n      timeout-minutes 50\n      reason \"Measured 41.3 minutes at most (macos-x64; windows-arm64 37.6): one release build plus Electron packaging per operating system, which one machine has to do. Pull requests run it only when desktop, vscode or Rust sources change. To meet 30: package a release binary built once per target.\"\n    over-limit-job cli\n      timeout-minutes 50\n      reason \"Measured 34.4 minutes at most (cli-macos-x64): one cold release build per target on the slowest runner. To meet 30: share the release build with the desktop job for the same target.\"\n  workflow \".github/workflows/external-benchmarks.yml\"\n    over-limit-job external-benchmarks\n      timeout-minutes 90\n      reason \"Schedule and dispatch only (skipped on pull requests, which run the ratchet): runs the upstream suites, 21.2 minutes at most on main. To meet 30: run the sharded upstream-shard path on schedule too.\"\n    over-limit-job upstream-shard\n      timeout-minutes 45\n      reason \"Dispatch with a shard size only: one window of the upstream suites. To meet 30: size the windows from measured durations.\"\n  workflow \".github/workflows/issue-1028-agent-ladder.yml\"\n    over-limit-job ladder\n      tim